      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm working on integrating a payment gateway via a REST API and im getting stuck. i keep getting a 402 Payment Required error in the json response, but i've checked the card details and they seem fine. what are the usual reasons for this error and how should i go about debugging the payload to see what's actually wrong?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The 402 Payment Required error usually means the payment method or amount specified in your API request is not sufficient or accepted. Double-check the API documentation for the required amount, payment method, or currency. Verify that your request payload matches the expected format and values, including currency, amount, and method (e.g., credit card, bank transfer). Additionally, look into the access token details to ensure it has not expired and that it's correctly included in your API request headers. Testing with different payment methods or amounts specified can also help identify the exact issue. For debugging, place all payload details in the body of the request if not already visible in the API UI and cross-check with the documentation.",
